    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="3fc8dd64-376a-59a1-81a8-3a9b814566f3" activityNameId="74490b59-0193-50bd-99ed-f733be89a8b9" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Pipeline, natural gas, long distance, high capacity, offshore</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Pipeline, natural gas, long distance, high capacity, offshore
It is assumed that all pipelines stays in the sea at the end of their lifetime. The weighted average life time of the pipeline is 45 years.;
UUID: a3b0ad50-a6b6-3dfa-bca2-5867a81fe0e7
This dataset describes the infrastructure needed for a long-distance undersea pipeline with a capacity from average 1.6 e6 Sm3/h gas including material requirements, construction, anode emissions and disposal.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: The quantity of steel and concrete is calculated for an average Norwegian North Sea pipeline (diameter 1000mm, thickness steel 25mm, thickness concrete 100mm).
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: environmental report 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_a3b0ad50-a6b6-3dfa-bca2-5867a81fe0e7.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="f4808887-5a57-5892-975e-ba0565a93e23" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
